Short:        Web browser written in 68k assembly
Author:       @AUTHOR@
Uploader:     @AUTHOR@
Type:         comm/www
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1.0
Requires:     68020+, Fast RAM, a TCP/IP stack, AmiSSL 6 for https
Kurz:         Webbrowser in 68k-Assembler geschrieben

Velox is a small, fast web browser for classic AmigaOS 3.x, written
entirely in 68k assembly. It stays responsive while pages load: the
page scrolls, and links, gadgets and menus work at once.

Features
--------

- HTML with a tolerant HTML5-style parser; UTF-8, Latin-1 and
  Windows-1252 pages
- CSS: selectors with specificity, colours, fonts, margins, padding,
  borders, widths, alignment, floats, media queries
- Tables, lists, forms (GET and POST), frames (each scrolling on its
  own), image maps, background images
- Images decoded by Velox itself: JPEG (also progressive), PNG, GIF and
  WebP, dithered to the screen's colours; other formats through the
  picture datatypes
- Tabs, each loading on its own, all at once
- http and https (AmiSSL 6, with certificate checks), keep-alive,
  cookies, a memory and a disk cache, Back and Forward from pages kept
  in memory or on disk, bookmarks, downloads, find in page, view
  source, selecting text to the clipboard
- Keyboard navigation for everything

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.1 or newer, a 68020 or better
- Fast RAM: with Chip RAM alone (a stock A1200) few pages fit. A few
  MB will do without https; with AmiSSL, 8 MB or more (AmiSSL alone
  takes about 4 MB)
- A TCP/IP stack with bsdsocket.library (Roadshow, AmiTCP, Miami...)
- For https: AmiSSL 6, or velox-proxy.py (included) running on another
  computer

Installing
----------

Copy the Velox drawer anywhere and start Velox from its icon or from a
Shell. Velox/Velox.guide (an AmigaGuide) tells the rest: the tool
types, the Shell arguments, the keys, tabs, https and the proxy.

Source
------

Velox is free software under the GNU General Public License version 3
(Velox/LICENSE). Its source is in Velox/Source, and at
https://github.com/johansmolinski/velox

Changes in @VERSION@
----------------

The first upload to Aminet. Since 0.1.1 on GitHub: tabs; logging in
with the keyboard (Tab goes on from a field clicked into, Return sends
the form as its submit button would); links styled as buttons look
like buttons (a background, padding and an outline behind inline
elements); text areas edited as in a notepad (the cursor anywhere,
lines wrapped, Shift selects, undo and redo); address completion (the
pages visited that match are listed under the address field as you
type); Velox.guide, this documentation as an AmigaGuide; icons in
MagicWB's colours.
